1
00:00:00,682 --> 00:00:04,682
(Penny:)I get it. Leonard has no business
being involved with a waitress/actress...

2
00:00:04,853 --> 00:00:09,403
(Penny:)...who felt so insecure, that she lied to him
about finishing community college.

3
00:00:09,566 --> 00:00:11,106
(Sheldon:)Why would you lie about that?

4
00:00:11,276 --> 00:00:14,026
He was going on about this college
and that grad school...

5
00:00:14,196 --> 00:00:17,696
(Penny:)...and I didn't want him to think
I was some kind of stupid loser.

6
00:00:17,866 --> 00:00:22,036
You thought the opposite of "stupid loser"
was "community-college graduate"?

7
00:00:26,917 --> 00:00:29,457
(Penny:)There are a lot of successful people
in this country...

8
00:00:29,628 --> 00:00:31,458
...who are community-college graduates.

9
00:00:31,630 --> 00:00:33,840
Yeah, but you are neither.

10
00:00:35,759 --> 00:00:38,049
(Penny:)Right. Okay, look,
this is between you and me.

11
00:00:38,220 --> 00:00:41,350
(Penny:)You cannot tell Leonard any of this.

12
00:00:42,516 --> 00:00:45,396
- You're asking me to keep a secret?
- Yeah.

13
00:00:45,561 --> 00:00:46,731
(Sheldon:)Well, I'm sorry.

14
00:00:46,895 --> 00:00:50,145
You would've had to express that desire
before revealing the secret...

15
00:00:50,315 --> 00:00:54,275
...so that I could choose whether I wanted
to accept the covenant of secret-keeping.

16
00:00:54,945 --> 00:00:59,025
(Sheldon:)You can't impose a secret
on an ex post facto basis.

